    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\n`packed_ipc_producer` drops the final chunk when the input contains only zero-element tensors. Flush when metadata is present so names, shapes, and dtypes survive a zero-byte payload.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Preserve metadata for one or more empty tensors with a one line predicate change.\n- Keep an empty iterator at zero chunks and preserve existing nonempty transfer behavior.\n- Add two parameterized CUDA regressions in the existing producer suite.\n\n## Validation\n\nGB10/SM121, Torch `2.13.0+cu130`. On main `f26d9f432ced7b1087d02d29bffed2249df1a18e`, the affected source and test file are byte identical to the original tested base `61f084b5f3e58aa3d3eb5c86aeaf4686c460c478`. The human submitter confirmed line review and explicitly requested this validation rerun; the agent executed the commands.\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Baseline with the two new CUDA regressions | 2 failed as expected, 29 deselected |\n| Proposed source with the complete existing test file | 31 passed, 10 warnings, 7.56 seconds |\n| Separate spawned CUDA consumer | 6 positive controls and 1 controlled abort passed; consumer exit 0 |\n| Full configured pre-commit hooks on both changed files | Passed; unrelated file types skipped normally |\n\nGPU tests used a bounded isolated launcher that loads the actual source module and upstream test file. `$PYTHON` below denotes the existing Torch/vLLM environment's `.venv/bin/python`:\n\n```bash\nD_EMPTY_VARIANT=baseline \"$PYTHON\" d_empty_fix_pytest.py\nD_EMPTY_VARIANT=fixed \"$PYTHON\" d_empty_fix_pytest.py\n\"$PYTHON\" d_fixed_ipc_envelope.py --directory . --output spawned-consumer.json\n```\n\nThe consumer checks cover empty-only metadata, an empty iterator, mixed empty/scalar tensors, delayed six-chunk owned-copy retention, abort, and recovery. Both proposed files match the GPU tested source bytes after formatting checks.\n\nThe fresh checkout also ran:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/pre-commit run --files \\\n  vllm/distributed/weight_transfer/packed_tensor.py \\\n  tests/distributed/test_packed_tensor.py\n```\n\nIn a full vLLM development environment, the included regression can be reproduced with `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/distributed/test_packed_tensor.py -k preserves_zero_sized_tensor_metadata`. The full checkout pytest command was not used for the recorded isolated fixture results.\n\n## Details\n\nEmpty tensors contribute metadata but zero bytes. The final `if total_bytes:` silently omits that logical transfer. `if names:` includes it while leaving a genuinely empty iterator unchanged. No API, dependency, or buffer ownership rule changes.\n\nThis is separate from alignment PR #57665, which fixes dtype views over unaligned slices. Bounded searches found no open exact empty-only producer fix. Broader searches returned unrelated kernel PRs #48580 and #46676; neither changes this module. RFC #59502 concerns modulewise reload and integrity.\n\nShared CUDA tensor teardown warnings remain visible in baseline and proposed runs. This patch does not claim to fix lifetime warnings, leaks, model accuracy, or serving performance. No model benchmark is presented for this transport metadata corner case.\n\nAI tools assisted with reproduction, the patch, tests, and PR preparation. Human line review was confirmed, and test execution was explicitly delegated to the agent. Direct human shell execution is not claimed.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull Request Checklist</summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill.\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n- [x] **Design Fit:** One final flush predicate changes; existing producer and test suite are reused.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Baseline failure, CUDA suite, and real spawned consumer checks validate the changed path. New tests remain in the existing CI-tethered file.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Full configured pre-commit hooks passed without skip overrides or unrelated edits.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Root cause, commands, results, related work, AI assistance, and limits are recorded.\n</details>\n\n",
